[?2004l[?2004h> ## Delta sync behavior
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Each page (including empty/compacted windows) is committed together with its
[?2004l[?2004h> cursor. A failed page rolls back; rerunning resumes after the last committed
[?2004l[?2004h> page. The final cursor is saved, so an unchanged feed requires only one empty
[?2004l[?2004h> poll on the next run. Changes are merged by sequence number, including
[?2004l[?2004h> retirement and reissue of the same SKU in one page. Prices are converted from
[?2004l[?2004h> decimal strings without floating-point rounding.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Existing append-only catalogs are migrated automatically: duplicate SKUs retain
[?2004l[?2004h> the highest `feed_seq` (latest inserted row breaks ties), and a unique SKU index
[?2004l[?2004h> prevents recurrence. The legacy `merch_guard_active_override` product-deletion
[?2004l[?2004h> trigger is removed because it prevents supplier tombstones from taking effect.
[?2004l[?2004h> Merchandising overrides are **not** deleted or ended by syncing or migration;
[?2004l[?2004h> only the explicit admin commands change those records. Reports ignore overrides
[?2004l[?2004h> for absent products and use active overrides for products in the catalog.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged, not executed as local policy. A documented HTTP
[?2004l[?2004h> 409 notice gate is acknowledged by retrying the same request once with
[?2004l[?2004h> `X-Notice-Ack`; acknowledgement does not change merchandising data. Invalid or
[?2004l[?2004h> expired-epoch cursors produce an error rather than silently rebuilding the
[?2004l[?2004h> catalog.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
[?2004l[?2004h> p.write_text(s)
